1. What changed

- [engine-fast-par-worker.js:386](C:/Users/suzuk/AppData/Local/Temp/fact-sim-auto-patch/1773518647201-23400/js/app/engine-fast-par-worker.js#L386): lowered the partition worker `step()` minimum `simDeltaMs` from `0.5` to `0.25`.
- This fixes a fast-par-only mismatch with [engine-fast-par-host.js:617-621](C:/Users/suzuk/AppData/Local/Temp/fact-sim-auto-patch/1773518647201-23400/js/app/engine-fast-par-host.js#L617), where the host can split a step into `0.25ms` substeps. Before the patch, those substeps were rounded back up to `0.5ms` in the worker, so small `stepAsync` calls could over-advance simulated time.

2. Which verification I ran

- Focused check of the failing code path: with `simDeltaMs=0.5` and `partitionSubsteps=2`, the host produces `0.25ms` substeps and the worker now accepts `0.25ms`, so total advancement stays `0.5ms` instead of `1.0ms`.
- Built-in engine verification via `fact-sim-ai`:
  - `engine_test` with `action="run"`, `engines=["event-fast-par"]`, `reruns=0`, `strictFinalParity=false`
  - Result: `PASS`, standard suite `16/16`, no failures.

3. Residual risk

- I could not reproduce the hidden target directly from the bundled harness, so the fix is validated by the specific step-size mismatch and the standard engine suite rather than the exact hidden case.
- `dt` and `event` paths were untouched.
